Bundle-Name: Model Atlas - GDPR Flow Analysis for QVT
Bundle-Description: Derives a GDPR report for a compiled QVT-O transformation from the reviews of \
 the metamodels it was compiled against (issue #319). A transformation is not reviewed, it is \
 derived: the analyser walks the compiled unit's AST, works out which source feature reaches which \
 target feature and how, and applies a fixed rule table to what the metamodel reviews already say \
 about those features.

# The case it exists for: a target field that is harmless on its own receives firstName, lastName
# and address concatenated into it. Neither model's own review can see that - only the
# transformation knows the three meet, and only there is it visible that a field-level
# classification has been folded into something that cannot be classified, minimised or erased
# per field.
#
# It reviews nothing. Every category it asserts was asserted by a model review first, and every
# citation is carried over from the review it came from, verbatim - the analyser never looks a
# provision up, so it can never invent one. Where no review exists it says so rather than coming
# back clean, which is why the subject lists a package with an unset reportId instead of omitting
# it.
#
# No provider, no key, no network: the whole analysis is a pure function of the stored compiled
# unit and the stored reports.

-workingset: ModelAtlas

-library: enableEMF

-buildpath: \
	org.eclipse.fennec.gdpr.report.model;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.action.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.scope.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.management;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.workflow;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.m2x.unit;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.m2x.qvto.model;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.m2x.ocl.model;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.util.promise;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.component;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.metatype.annotations;version=latest

# junit-jupiter-api alone, the way the sibling gdpr bundles have it: the engine and the platform
# launcher come from the workspace build.gradle, and putting bnd's copies of them here as well
# mixes two versions of the platform - at which point the engine discovers no tests at all.
#
# The other two are what reading a stored compiled unit needs outside OSGi: XMI, and qvtbase,
# which the imperative OCL package initialises against.
-testpath: \
	junit-jupiter-api,\
	org.eclipse.emf.ecore.xmi,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.m2x.qvt.model;version=latest

-privatepackage: org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.qvt.gdpr

javac.source: 21
javac.target: 21

Bundle-Version: 1.0.0.SNAPSHOT
